# direnv's own `use flake` — no nix-direnv needed. It keeps the dev shell in a
# nix profile under .direnv, which doubles as the GC root.
#
# The mkdir is direnv >= 2.37's `use_flake` doing this itself; older direnv
# doesn't, and then `nix print-dev-env --profile .direnv/flake-profile` fails on
# a fresh clone because .direnv doesn't exist yet. Harmless once it does.
mkdir -p "$(direnv_layout_dir)"

use flake
